finding: Medium — the public `bin/shallot.ts` wrapper turns the test runner's signal death into an ordinary exit 1. `bun /tmp/shallot-review-caller-probe.ts` targeted SIGTERM only at the nested runner: `bin` returned `exitValue:1, exitCode:1, signalCode:null`, while `bun run test` returned `exitValue:143, exitCode:null, signalCode:"SIGTERM"`. `bin/shallot.ts` uses `Bun.spawnSync` then `process.exit(proc.exitCode ?? 1)`, discarding `proc.signalCode`; the CLI caller therefore cannot distinguish cancellation from a test failure. It should restore/re-raise the child's signal rather than normalize it to a status.
